<!--
    THE SHORTCUT RECORDER

    A read-only field that captures the next key chord pressed into it, rejects the
    ones this app cannot register, and reports what it captured. It writes nothing:
    the host decides where the shortcut goes, which is the only reason it can serve
    all THREE hosts, SEVEN boxes between them:

      - Settings > Shortcuts, five of them, straight into SettingsService;
      - Settings > Streaming, one, editing the SAME setting as the Shortcuts page's
        Streaming box - the second editor nobody had fixed, which is what #794 was;
      - the onboarding Permissions step, one, through the flow model's seam so the
        registration row refreshes and the flow-model suite stays WPF-free.

    A change to this control's behaviour lands on all seven. Count them again before
    you write a number into a comment here; this block has been wrong once already.

    Extracted, not written. Every line of the capture and the validation came off
    ShortcutsSettingsPage.xaml.cs, which was where the ONLY recorder in this app
    lived: a bare TextBox plus two PreviewKey handlers, wired to five named boxes by
    a Tag string and five named error TextBlocks. That is not reusable in place, and
    copying it for onboarding would have made two recorders that could drift on what
    counts as a legal shortcut. There is still exactly one.

    The field is IsReadOnly and swallows KeyUp as well as KeyDown, so a Win-key
    release never leaks into WPF text input while the global hook is live.

    Focus ARRIVING and focus LEAVING are both boundaries of a gesture, and they are
    not symmetric: see Field_GotKeyboardFocus and Field_LostKeyboardFocus in the
    code-behind for what each one clears and what each one deliberately does not.
-->
<UserControl x:Class="HyperWhisper.Views.Controls.ShortcutRecorderBox"
             xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml">
    <StackPanel>
        <TextBox x:Name="Field"
                 Padding="10,6"
                 Background="{DynamicResource InputBackgroundBrush}"
                 Foreground="{DynamicResource TextPrimaryBrush}"
                 BorderBrush="{DynamicResource BorderBrush}"
                 IsReadOnly="True"
                 VerticalAlignment="Center"
                 PreviewKeyDown="Field_PreviewKeyDown"
                 PreviewKeyUp="Field_PreviewKeyUp"
                 GotKeyboardFocus="Field_GotKeyboardFocus"
                 LostKeyboardFocus="Field_LostKeyboardFocus"/>

        <TextBlock x:Name="ErrorText"
                   Text=""
                   Foreground="{DynamicResource ErrorForegroundBrush}"
                   FontSize="11"
                   Margin="0,4,0,0"
                   Visibility="Collapsed"
                   TextWrapping="Wrap"/>
    </StackPanel>
</UserControl>
